# 02 DFA matching: pcre2_dfa_match()
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2matching.html
#
# Not exposed by PHP.
#
# What it is: PCRE2 ships a second matching engine. pcre2_dfa_match()
# scans the subject once and tracks all alternatives in parallel. There is
# no backtracking. It reports ALL matches that start at the match point
# (longest first) and it can suspend at the end of one buffer and resume
# in the next. Capture groups are not supported. \=dfa selects the engine
# in pcre2test.
#
# What it enables: leftmost-longest ("POSIX") semantics and "every
# alternative that matches here" queries. It also streams over chunked
# input. And since nothing backtracks, the patterns it accepts cannot
# blow up.

# Every alternative that matches at one starting point

# Expect: 0: abc
#         1: ab
#         2: a
# One call reports every alternative matching at the same start position.
# The regular engine reports only the first alternative that succeeds.
/a|ab|abc/
    abc\=dfa

# Streaming: one match across two chunks

# Expect: Partial match: dogsb
#         0: ody
# The first chunk ends mid-match (hard partial). The second call picks up
# where the first stopped, in a completely new buffer. The two subjects
# below are ONE match split over two chunks.
/dogsbody/
    dogsb\=dfa,ps
    ody\=dfa,dfa_restart
